/* ============================================================================
   SABA Virtual Assistant - Questions & Answers data
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   All of the assistant's content lives in the single JSON object assigned to
   `qaData` below (the value itself is pure JSON).

   This is a .js file rather than a .json file only so that the pages keep
   working when opened directly from disk (file://), where browsers block
   fetching .json files. No backend or web server is required.

   HOW TO EDIT
   - Each question/answer pair is one object in the "questions" array.
   - Fields:
       id         : sequential number (informational only)
       category   : unique category identifier (e.g., "Learner", "Manager", "Admin", etc.)
       categoryEN : (optional) category display name in English (defaults to category if not specified)
       categoryFR : (optional) category display name in French (defaults to category if not specified)
       questionEN : the question shown in English
       questionFR : the question shown in French
       keywordsEN : comma-separated search keywords (English)
       keywordsFR : comma-separated search keywords (French)
       answerEN   : the answer shown in English (may contain HTML tags)
       answerFR   : the answer shown in French (may contain HTML tags)
   - Answers support HTML (<p>, <a>, <strong>, <ul>, <ol>, <table>, <br>...).
   - Inside a value, double quotes must be escaped as \" (e.g. href=\"...\").
   - Keep entries separated by commas; the last entry has no trailing comma.
   - To add a question: copy an existing block, give it the next id, and fill
     in the eight fields. The order of entries is the order used by the app.
   ============================================================================ */
